    "result": "P ≈ exp(-sqrt(E_G / E)), where E_G = 2 * mu * (pi * alpha * Z1 * Z2)^2 * c^2, with mu being the reduced mass and alpha the fine-structure constant."
  },
  "part_2": {
    "description": "Fusion reaction rate per unit volume",
    "formula": "R = n_D * n_T * <sigma * v>",
    "explanation": [
      "The reaction rate is defined by R = n_D * n_T * integral(sigma(v) * v * f(v) dv).",
      "The cross-section sigma(E) includes the tunneling probability (Gamow factor) P(E) multiplied by a geometric factor (1/E) and the nuclear astrophysical S-factor.",
      "Integration over the Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution f(E, T) yields the Gamow peak, where the integrand is dominated by the product of the exponential decay of the tunneling probability and the exponential decay of the Maxwellian tail."
    ]
  }
}
```

